{
  "pr_number": 218,
  "title": "REQ-118: cache resolved permissions per role",
  "repo": "acme/cms-core",
  "provenance": "simulated",
  "issue": {
    "number": 118,
    "title": "Permission resolution adds 40ms to every request",
    "body": "# REQ-118 \u2014 Cache resolved permissions per role\n\n**Issue:** #118\n**Component:** auth\n**Priority:** P2 \u2014 latency on every authenticated request\n\nScope: auth/cache.py\n\n## Problem\n\nPermission resolution adds 40ms to every request. `api/middleware.py` calls\n`resolve_permissions()` on every authenticated route, and every call is a round\ntrip to the role store. Roles change a few times a week; we are paying for a\nfresh lookup thousands of times a second.\n\n## Requirement\n\nCache resolved permissions per role for 60 seconds.\n\n- Key the cache by role id.\n- 60 second TTL. `auth/cache.py` already defines `DEFAULT_TTL_S`.\n- A hit must return exactly what the store would have returned.\n- Provide a way to drop a role's entry when its grants change.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n`auth/permissions.py` and `api/middleware.py` keep their current behaviour.\nThis ticket is the cache only.\n\n## Done when\n\n- A second resolve of the same role inside 60 seconds does not hit the store.\n- After 60 seconds the store is consulted again.\n- `pytest` passes.\n",
    "url": "https://github.com/acme/cms-core/issues/118"
  },
  "reviews": [
    {
      "reviewer": "rdolan",
      "state": "APPROVED",
      "ask_to_approve_s": 1320
    }
  ],
  "review_comments": [
    {
      "reviewer": "rdolan",
      "path": "auth/cache.py",
      "line": 62,
      "body": "Is 60s right for a role that was just revoked? What drops the entry?"
    },
    {
      "reviewer": "rdolan",
      "path": "auth/cache.py",
      "line": 74,
      "body": "Please don't cache the empty set as a hit -- an unknown role isn't a miss."
    },
    {
      "reviewer": "rdolan",
      "path": "api/middleware.py",
      "line": 52,
      "body": "This still returns 503 on a store error, right? Confirm we didn't change that."
    }
  ],
